
# The `view` role: the grammar of a sandboxed document, the dialect a page or a guide is written in.
#
# Four statement heads reach the mill and not one of them declares anything the author wrote. `load` reaches the
# approved catalogs, `host` names a constant or a parameter the route fills, `find` names a query the host
# resolves before rendering, and `view` defines the document.
#
#   load @view/text
#     find heading
#
#   host slug, like text
#   host title, text <How Quenya sounds>
#
#   find vowel
#     task <filter:phoneme>
#     meet and
#       hold is-equal
#         read self/kind
#         text <vowel>
#     sort rise, read self/height
#
#   view page
#     view text/heading
#       bind text, read title
#
# `tree` and `fuse` are the fifth head and its use site, and neither appears here. A macro is expanded on the
# parse tree by `compile/template.ts` before any mill runs, so by the time this grammar reads a file the macros
# are gone and their bodies stand where each `fuse` was. See note/term/view/02-macro.md.
#
# What the mill will NOT build is as much the point as what it will. The body reuses the component AST, which can
# express things a document may not have, so this grammar has no way to reach `view-save` (a computed local),
# `view-seed` (an attribute or an event handler), or a `walk` whose mode is `test`. See note/term/view/05-sandbox.md.

load @term/mill/code/view/load/mine
  find view-load

load @term/mill/code/view/host/mine
  find view-host

load @term/mill/code/view/find/mine
  find view-find

load @term/mill/code/view/def/mine
  find view-def

mine view-file
  mine list
    mine any
      mine form, like view-load
        site load
      mine form, like view-host
        site host
      mine form, like view-find
        site find
      mine form, like view-def
        site view
